# Never commit secrets, local Terraform state, or pipeline outputs.
# NOTE: git ignore-rules do NOT support trailing inline comments - a '#' only
# starts a comment at the start of a line. Keep every pattern on its own line.

# your real values (DO token, Spaces keys, domain)
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
# downloaded provider binaries
.terraform/
# !! contains every resource attribute in plaintext, incl. the Spaces keys
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# --- pipeline outputs (maps-region-delivery.md §9: do NOT check in .pmtiles) ---
# The planet + per-region extracts are large binaries built out-of-band and published to
# Spaces; they never belong in the tree (the ~1.3 MB bundled Firenze demo in
# ui-map/src/androidMain/assets/ stays the only PMTiles binary in-tree).
build/
*.pmtiles
catalog.json
catalog.json.sig

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is intentionally NOT ignored - commit it after the first
# `terraform init` so every apply resolves the same provider plugins/hashes (HashiCorp's
# recommended practice). It is absent here only because init can't run in the authoring env.
